Moybyte's changes to Dropbear, all under DROPBEAR_MOY (port/localoptions.h):
the server runs inside the kernel's process, one session at a time.

- sysoptions.h: the tracking allocator is on, so a session's allocations
  are freed with its epoch when it ends (moy_ssh.c).
- dbmalloc.c: the allocator's calloc/realloc/free are DB_CALLOC/DB_REALLOC/
  DB_FREE, PSRAM and counted on a board (port/moy_ssh_port.h).
- svr-session.c: an exit jumps back to the accept loop instead of exit();
  the log is moy_ssh_log; no unauthenticated close delay (one task).
- common-session.c: no signal pipe; the command's end is polled every loop.
- svr-chansession.c: no fork, no pty, no SIGCHLD: a session's command is
  moy_ssh_command (the shell's face over a socket pair), its end
  moy_ssh_reap, its signal moy_ssh_signal; a pty request keeps the size.
- chansession.h: the size a pty request asked for.
- dbrandom.c: the seed is the SoC's hardware generator (moy_ssh_entropy).
- gensignkey.c: the host key is renamed into place (FAT has no link()).
- svr-kex.c: the made-key log's fingerprint only where the build has it
  (DROPBEAR_SIGNKEY_VERIFY): a server without public-key sign-in does not.
- libtomcrypt's crypt_cipher_descriptor.c and crypt_hash_descriptor.c: the
  tables are PSRAM, taken at setup (port/moy_ssh_port.h), not .bss.

